          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:63555e80e4aa924141247dcc04909d7fa8f4740b1caf16ca748b5e651278dfc2:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_86fdcc7cb22443f7a389ad0a1459ed66",
      "statement": "Inertialized hips blending across a rootPositionsMask change and toe-floor penetration correction were dropped when the pipeline moved to stages and are both still absent; the intended home for each is a MoSynthStage running after the pose is produced rather than another special case inside the orchestrator.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Core/MotionSynthesisComponent.cs#L293-L297",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:accd251de68f2ca8bfe0fd3911cfab5e64ffed0a021aa53f4a48f7fc198ea998:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f8435de4b3c04b4ca85258a3ce3063d2",
      "statement": "Advancing the character's Transform by the frame's own velocity is gated on the rootPositionsMask flag; when it is off the pose is still applied and bone 0 is still placed frame-locally, but the Transform is never integrated, so the character animates in place instead of travelling.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Core/MotionSynthesisComponent.cs#L286-L323",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:d5f5e5235ded88e3b6fc887d7c5d78d16d7508bdc8231c8fe2ed439350afb16d:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e3792819d674407b9f33ff865df7a0ab",
      "statement": "Applying a pose writes bone 0's local position and rotation but writes only the local rotation of every other bone — their local positions are never touched — so bone lengths come from the scene rig's own Transforms rather than from the pose.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Core/MotionSynthesisComponent.cs#L268-L285",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:097494c21d3a5b3159ca9b7ca87d2039d9432e99df3f82e49c3a4c6cc4d1c216:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_e7d5a8c9b752423dbdea73225a077613",
      "statement": "The component applies the pose regardless of what any stage returned or whether any stage ran, so the values read off the rig reach the apply step on several reachable paths — an empty or entirely disabled stage list, the ZeroMQ connector returning without a reply, and the motion field stage after a mid-run exception.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://Assets/AnimationTools/Runtime/Core/MotionSynthesisComponent.cs#L186-L212",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:19a11fe4c15e81770f928cf13bb8a67a9b45553bcd252f4761c379f9444beb8f:"
